<Layout title="About the Archive" active="About">
  <section class="detail-hero"><div class="page-wrap"><p class="kicker">Administrative note // please post more</p><h1>About<br />the archive</h1><p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">This is the crew’s unofficial record of a very official fight against the Empire, interrupted by theft, repairs, and an unreasonable number of explosions.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="page-wrap"><div class="about-grid"><article class="plate about-card"><p class="kicker">Webmaster’s statement</p><h3>Deech built this between meditation sessions.</h3><p>Everyone else was asleep. DV-8 was not, because DV-8 does not sleep and has opinions about build tooling. Deech used the quiet hour to assemble the archive and would like it noted that the rest of the crew could contribute to the travelogue more often.</p><p>There are heroic deeds in this galaxy. Posting a paragraph is one of them.</p></article><article class="plate about-card"><p class="kicker">Editorial policy</p><h3>Role-play mode: permanent.</h3><p>Everything here stays in-universe, with a straight face that may wobble under pressure. Campaign details draw from Dawn of Defiance and from events as remembered by the people who survived them.</p><p>Errors may be reported to the nearest Jedi, engineer, or person who looks like they know what they are doing.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="page-wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">Source trail</p><h2>Built from scraps,<br />kept by witnesses.</h2></div><p>The Mandalorian system supplies the battered plates, burnt-orange clan mark, mono telemetry, and practical hierarchy. The campaign material covers Dawn of Defiance Parts 1–6. The crew supplies the disputed facts.</p></div><div class="log-list"><div class="log-entry"><span class="date">SYSTEM</span><div><h3>Mandalorian design system</h3><p>Battle-worn, pragmatic, clan-oriented, rugged, utilitarian. No gloss. No soft edges. No unnecessary decoration.</p></div><span class="place">sw-design</span></div><div class="log-entry"><span class="date">CAMPAIGN</span><div><h3>Dawn of Defiance 01—06</h3><p>Sel Zonn Station, Felucia, Cato Neimoidia, Bespin, Almas, Nizon, Coruscant, and the first six steps toward the Sarlacc Project.</p></div><span class="place">archive source</span></div></div></div></section>
</Layout>
